<!--
  era1_1.tmx — the hand-built reference level for Phase 4's loader
  (GAMEPLAY-V2.md Section 11).

  This map is the one authored by hand; the other 42 are generated against
  this exact schema afterwards. It deliberately exercises every feature the
  loader has to support, in an order that makes a failure easy to localise:

    - ground with two real gaps (the first fall-damage test the game has
      ever had, since the old GroundSpawner laid one unbroken slab)
    - a one-way platform over each gap, 104-112 above the ground surface:
      above every enemy hit area (99.9) and under the jump peak (128)
    - artifact -> gate -> artifact ordering, so the player always meets a
      charge source before a blocker (the Phase 3 invariant)
    - walker and heavy enemies
    - coins both on the ground and on a platform
    - spawn and exit markers

  Geometry
  --------
  16px tiles, 45 rows = 720px — matches GameConstants.virtualHeight, so map
  y and world y are the same number and the loader needs no vertical
  remapping. Ground band is 60px (GroundSection.bandHeight), so the ground
  SURFACE is y=660 and occupies rows 41-44.

  Heights are measured in Tiled's y-down pixels:
    ground surface      y = 660
    platform at +108    y = 552
    platform at +112    y = 548
  Keep platforms inside 104-112: higher is out of reach of the jump (peak
  128), lower lets an enemy touch a student standing on one.

  Entity x positions are world x directly. The player spawns at x=220
  (GameConstants.playerX) so the opening frame matches the old spawner's.
-->
